//Anomen uses third CN line

@0 /*Keldorn*/ = ~You plan to attack a temple of the Radiant Heart, <CHARNAME>? You know I cannot let that stand.~
@1 /*CHARNAME*/ = ~Keldorn, my friend, you need to lighten up. Don't you know a joke when you hear one?~
@2 /*CHARNAME*/ = ~Relax, Keldorn. It was a plan, barely that... 'twas but the first tiny inkling of a scheme, if not less, the barest sketch of the notion of the vague possibility of a plot. So this one doesn't come to fruition. I'll live. I've got others.~
@3 /*CHARNAME*/ = ~You can't let that stand? Then I can't let you stand. Draw your blade!~

//After Anomen fails test
@4 /*CHARNAME*/ = ~Someday, Anomen, but not yet. We are not yet strong enough to prevail.~
@5 /*Anomen*/ = ~*sigh* You are right as usual, <CHARNAME>. Let us go forth. The Order's day of reckoning can wait.~

//An interjection into the fallen paladin quest.
@6 /*Anomen*/ = ~It seems the oppressive rules of the Order can break even their most dedicated lackeys.~

@8 /*Charname*/ = ~Calm down...~
@9 /*Anomen*/ = ~Leave me be! You saw it too! They shelter those scum rather than acknowledge that I avenged my sister! What kind of justice is this? What kind of order?~
@10 /*Clara*/ = ~*steps forward* I saw. I saw a brother do what had to be done for his sister. It was not a crime, Anomen. It was justice.~
@11 /*Anomen*/ = ~Justice? Ha! They called me a villain! Said I am unworthy of the Order's trust! They care nothing for me, and even less for Moira!~
@12 /*Clara*/ = ~Because they are blind. They sit in their towers clutching moldy regulations, having long forgotten what those regulations were written to protect. You remembered Moira. You settled her blood-debt—that is far more real than their seals and sashes.~
@13 /*Anomen*/ = ~*panting* I... I only wanted her to rest. The others deserved it too... they sheltered the murderer, they were guilty as well!~
@14 /*Clara*/ = ~Of course. To shelter evil is to be evil. You merely carried out true judgment—the judgment they lacked the courage to perform.~
@15 /*Anomen*/ = ~But... I am nothing now. Dishonorably cast out from the Order... I am nothing.~
@16 /*Clara*/ = ~No. You still have yourself. You still have the Delryn name. You still have your sword. *pause* And you still have time.~
@17 /*Anomen*/ = ~Time? Ha, I will not wait! I will charge in and butcher those who sheltered the guilty!~
@18 /*Clara*/ = ~Listen. If you charge in now, you only prove them right—that you are a madman beyond control. But if you turn around, live, and climb higher than they ever could... one day, you will sit above them and write those regulations yourself. Then who would dare cast you out?~
@19 /*Anomen*/ = ~*long silence* ...Climb higher.~
@20 /*Clara*/ = ~As long as you live, anything is possible. Die here, and you truly are garbage. Walk away alive, and one day they will kneel and beg you to return.~
@21 /*Anomen*/ = ~*deep breath* ...You are right. I cannot fall here. I will show them—without their approval, Anomen Delryn is still Anomen Delryn. One day... one day I shall return, and they will tremble at the memory of this decision.~
@22 /*Clara*/ = ~*smiles* There is the Anomen I know. Come. Let us leave this damned place behind. They are all watching.~